## What shipped (this session)

19 standalone Angular components at frontend/src/app/ui/, each in its
own folder (component.ts + index.ts). All use signals for state,
ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush, and thin-wrap theme.css classes for
styling — no competing design tokens, no inline styles that override the
locked theme.

- button: variants primary/secondary/ghost/danger/icon, sizes sm/md/lg
- card: padding variants, hover variant
- badge: variants neutral/success/warning/danger/info/premium
- kpi-card: label + value + gradient text + icon slot
- progress: track + fill, color variants, clamps to 0-100
- avatar: sm/md/lg/xl, derives initials from name input
- skeleton: width + height inputs, uses .skeleton class
- empty-state: title + message + icon slot + cta slot
- tier-badge: maps tier enum to badge variant (observer/contributor/
  vetted/governor/founder → neutral/info/success/warning/premium)
- modal: overlay + chrome, closeOnOverlay option, role=dialog
- stepper: numbered steps with done/active/done states, dividers
- toast: success/error/info variants, fixed positioning, dismiss
- tabs: pill-style tab group with role=tablist + aria-selected
- table: scroll wrapper, columns with format/align, .table-row per row
- switch: aria-checked toggle, click toggles
- accordion: title + body, chevron rotation when open
- vote-button: approve/reject states, click-to-toggle
- sparkline: SVG path, accepts values array + width/height
- stat-bar: animated fill (queueMicrotask triggers transition on mount
  so the fill animates from 0 to value instead of jumping — this was
  the bug caught by the user on 2026-08-11 in the previous scaffold
  attempt)

19 Playwright specs at frontend/e2e/ui-*.spec.ts. Each spec asserts
computed theme.css token values (font-weight 300 for kpi-number,
border-radius 14px for card, rgb(168,106,45) for badge-premium, etc.).
Each spec also exercises interactive state — clicks toggle the
switch, modal opens/closes, accordion expands, etc.

frontend/src/app/ui/index.ts is the barrel export — pages import the
primitives from `../../ui`.

frontend/src/app/pages/dashboard/dashboard.component.ts is now a
primitives showcase, not the wireframe port. The wireframe port is
pack 3. The showcase has every primitive rendered at least once so
the visual review at the end is meaningful.

