## What is deliberately NOT done

A. Shell. Pack 2. Sidebar + top bar + mobile bar + theme toggle +
   shell-layout. Each shell component gets its own Playwright spec.

B. Full dashboard port from wireframe/meridian/dashboard/. Pack 3.
   The current dashboard is the primitives showcase, not the wireframe
   port. Pack 3 ports the 4-KPI-row + Active Executions + Latest
   Opportunities + Pool Health + Portfolio layout from the wireframe
   using the primitives from pack 1 and shell from pack 2.

C. Wireframe verbatim match. Not achieved yet. The primitives match
   the theme tokens and the visual-fidelity-check skill's stage 2
   passes, but the dashboard page itself is not a wireframe port — it
   is a primitives showcase. Pack 3 is where the wireframe port
   happens.

D. Remaining 18 wireframe pages. Same as before — each becomes a
   per-domain feature pipeline pack (identity, communities,
   opportunities, executions, money, governance).

## Known issues that are NOT to be fixed in the next session

- Sass @import deprecation warning. Migrate styles.scss to @use /
  @forward in a future session.
- icon-library gap (Lucide icons via data-lucide in wireframe). The
  primitives use plain text symbols (↗, ⚡, $, ×, ▾, ✓, ✗) for now.
  Deferred to the first pack that consumes a data-lucide page.

Both are documented in the PRD-TRD as named follow-ups.

## Lessons learned (also recorded in sessions/decisions.md)

1. theme.css defines `--gradient-*` as SOLID COLOR values (#a86a2d
   for violet, etc.), not linear-gradients. The naming is misleading.
   Tests that check "background contains gradient" fail — assertions
   should check exact rgb values.

2. For Angular standalone components, host-level attributes go in
   the @Component `host` metadata, not in the template. The selector
   element doesn't render template attrs as its own attrs.

3. `<ui-button>` selector means tests must locate the inner `<button>`
   element to inspect button-specific props. The component selector
   matches the host element, not the rendered button.

